@@ -103,26 +103,26 @@ Justice Scalia opened with a memorable rebuke: ``The Court has mistaken a \texti
 \begin{quote}
 ``One century ago, the first Justice Harlan admonished this Court that the Constitution `neither knows nor tolerates classes among citizens.' \textit{Plessy v. Ferguson}, 163 U.S. 537, 559 (1896) (dissenting opinion). Unheeded then, those words now are understood to state a commitment to the law's neutrality where the rights of persons are at stake.''
 \end{quote}
-\noindent--- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court, \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 623} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
+\noindent --- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court, \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 623} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
 
 \begin{quote}
 ``A law declaring that in general it shall be more difficult for one group of citizens than for all others to seek aid from the government is itself a denial of equal protection of the laws in the most literal sense.''
 \end{quote}
-\noindent--- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court, \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 633} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
+\noindent --- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court, \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 633} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
 
 \begin{quote}
 ``[I]f the constitutional conception of `equal protection of the laws' means anything, it must at the very least mean that a bare \dots{} desire to harm a politically unpopular group cannot constitute a legitimate governmental interest.''
 \end{quote}
-\noindent--- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court (quoting \textit{Department of Agriculture v. Moreno}, 413 U.S. 528, 534 (1973)), \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 634--35} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
+\noindent --- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court (quoting \textit{Department of Agriculture v. Moreno}, 413 U.S. 528, 534 (1973)), \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 634--35} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
 
 \begin{quote}
 ``We must conclude that Amendment 2 classifies homosexuals not to further a proper legislative end but to make them unequal to everyone else. This Colorado cannot do. A State cannot so deem a class of persons a stranger to its laws.''
 \end{quote}
-\noindent--- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court, \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 635} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
+\noindent --- Justice Kennedy, Opinion of the Court, \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 635} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
 
 \begin{quote}
 ``The Court has mistaken a \textit{Kulturkampf} for a fit of spite. The constitutional amendment before us here is not the manifestation of a ``bare \dots{} desire to harm'' homosexuals, \textit{ante}, at 634, but is rather a modest attempt by seemingly tolerant Coloradans to preserve traditional sexual mores against the efforts of a politically powerful minority to revise those mores through use of the laws.''
 \end{quote}
-\noindent--- Justice Scalia, dissenting (joined by Chief Justice Rehnquist and Justice Thomas), \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 636} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
+\noindent --- Justice Scalia, dissenting (joined by Chief Justice Rehnquist and Justice Thomas), \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/517/620/}{517 U.S. at 636} (\href{https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/118027/romer-v-evans/}{CourtListener}).
 
 \end{document}
