-    \end{quote}
-    \item \textbf{The Constitutional Indian-Law Bargain (Gorsuch, J., concurring):}
-    \begin{quote}
-        ``Our Constitution reserves for the Tribes a place---an enduring place---in the structure of American life. It promises them sovereignty for as long as they wish to keep it. And it secures that promise by divesting States of authority over Indian affairs and by giving the federal government certain significant (but limited and enumerated) powers aimed at building a lasting peace.'' (\href{https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/21-376}{Cornell LII})
