-    \item \textbf{Supreme Court Follow-On Cases (2025):} Echoing Justice Barrett's concurrence on foreign corporate control, \textit{TikTok Inc. v. Garland}, 604 U.S. 56 (2025) (\href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/604/24-656/}{Justia}), upheld Congress's divest-or-ban statute under intermediate scrutiny, reaffirming that foreign organizations operating abroad lack First Amendment rights. In \textit{Free Speech Coalition, Inc. v. Paxton}, 606 U.S. 461 (2025) (\href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/606/23-1122/}{Justia}), the Court cited \textit{Moody}, 603 U.S. at 733, for the rule that First Amendment principles do not vary with new media, while upholding Texas's online age-verification law for sexually explicit content obscene to minors.
