-\end{itemize}
 
-\section{Key Quotations}
+\item \textbf{Extension to Parental Notification of Gender Transition:} On March 2, 2026, in \href{https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/25A810}{\textit{Mirabelli v. Bonta}, 607 U.S. 492 (2026) (per curiam)} (\href{https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/25pdf/607us2r17_bqmc.pdf}{SupremeCourt.gov}), the Court vacated a Ninth Circuit stay and reinstated an injunction blocking California school policies that barred staff from disclosing a student's social gender transition to parents without student consent. Relying squarely on \textit{Mahmoud}, the Court held that concealing a child's gender transition imposes an even ``greater'' intrusion on parents' Free Exercise and Fourteenth Amendment substantive due process rights and likely fails \textit{Mahmoud}'s strict scrutiny.
 
+\end{itemize}
