-\section{Case Metadata}
-
-\begin{itemize}
-  \item \textbf{Case Name:} \textit{United States v. Brown}, 381 U.S. 437 (1965) (85 S. Ct. 1707; 14 L. Ed. 2d 484).
-  \item \textbf{Briefing Book Placement:} Chapter 3: Federal Legislative Power (Article I, \S~9, cl. 3 --- Bill of Attainder Clause).
-  \item \textbf{Dates:} Argued March 29, 1965; Decided June 7, 1965.
-  \item \textbf{Lower Court:} Certiorari to the U.S. Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit (\textit{Brown v. United States}, 334 F.2d 488 (9th Cir. 1964) (en banc), reversing conviction in the U.S. District Court for the Northern District of California).
-  \item \textbf{Vote:} 5--4, affirming the Ninth Circuit's judgment dismissing the indictment.
-  \item \textbf{Majority Opinion:} Chief Justice Earl Warren, joined by Justices Hugo L. Black, William O. Douglas, William J. Brennan, Jr., and Arthur J. Goldberg.
-  \item \textbf{Concurring Opinions:} None.
