-\section{Doctrinal Significance and Modern Legacy (Through 2026)}
-
-\textit{Tennessee Wine} reshaped both Twenty-first Amendment doctrine and broader Dormant Commerce Clause jurisprudence. First, it decisively settled the post-\textit{Granholm} circuit split over whether the Dormant Commerce Clause's antidiscrimination principle reaches the wholesale and retail tiers of state alcohol markets: it does, and States cannot insulate protectionist licensing barriers by invoking \S~2. Second, Justice Alito's robust defense of the Dormant Commerce Clause's historical legitimacy anchored the Court's antidiscrimination core even as a fractured Court later narrowed the extraterritoriality and \textit{Pike} balancing branches in \href{https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/598/21-468/}{\textit{National Pork Producers Council v. Ross}, 598 U.S. 356 (2023)}.
