-\begin{itemize}
-  \item \textbf{Hypothetical 1 (Post-Filing Voluntary Cessation):} A state environmental group whose members regularly kayak on Buffalo Bayou sues a chemical plant under CWA \S~505 while the plant is actively exceeding its benzene permit limits, seeking civil penalties payable to the Treasury. Six months into discovery, the plant installs new scrubbers, achieves full compliance, and moves to dismiss as moot. \textit{Analysis:} Under \textit{Laidlaw} and \textit{FBI v. Fikre}, the group had standing at filing (curtailed recreational use plus ongoing violations redressable by deterrent civil penalties), and the plant's post-filing compliance does not moot the case unless the plant proves it is ``absolutely clear'' that benzene violations cannot reasonably be expected to recur.
