-\begin{quote}
-``In an agency case as in any other, though, even if some judges might (or might not) consider the statute ambiguous, there is a best reading all the same---`the reading the court would have reached' if no agency were involved. \textit{Chevron}, 467 U.S., at 843, n. 11. It therefore makes no sense to speak of a `permissible' interpretation that is not the one the court, after applying all relevant interpretive tools, concludes is best. In the business of statutory interpretation, if it is not the best, it is not permissible.''\\
---- Chief Justice Roberts, \href{https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/22-451}{603 U.S. at 400}
-\end{quote}
