+
+Justice Stewart agreed with the judgment and much of the opinion, but rejected any ``uncritical assumption'' that children's First Amendment rights are coextensive with adults' rights, citing his concurrence in \textit{Ginsberg v. New York}, 390 U.S. 629 (1968), that children may lack the full capacity for individual choice presupposed by the First Amendment.
